{"chunk_id":"RAG_PU_1993_HW_3DO","publication_year":1993,"chunk_type":"HARDWARE_ARC","title":"3DO","text":"Across the five issues, 3DO moves from extraordinary future-facing claims, through explicit skepticism about demonstrations and hype, to a real Netherlands hands-on encounter that causes PU to revise its earlier caution. This is a synthesis inference, not a single contemporaneous PU verdict.","authority":"DERIVED_YEAR_SYNTHESIS","epistemic_status":"INFERENCE_FROM_CHRONOLOGICAL_PRIMARY_EVIDENCE","evidence":[{"issue_id":"PU_001","pdf_page":10,"layer":"BEST_MACHINE_TRANSCRIPT_BY_PAGE","source_file":"auth/PU1/BLACKPAPER_PU_001_COMPLETE_ARCHIVE_v2/raw_text/PU_001_BEST_MACHINE_TRANSCRIPT_BY_PAGE.jsonl","note":null},{"issue_id":"PU_001","pdf_page":11,"layer":"BEST_MACHINE_TRANSCRIPT_BY_PAGE","source_file":"auth/PU1/BLACKPAPER_PU_001_COMPLETE_ARCHIVE_v2/raw_text/PU_001_BEST_MACHINE_TRANSCRIPT_BY_PAGE.jsonl","note":null},{"issue_id":"PU_002","pdf_pages":[16],"layer":"ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE","knowledge_id":"PU_002_KNOW_007","source_file":"auth/PU2/PU_002_COMPLETE_INGEST/PU_002_ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE.jsonl","source_authority":"DIRECT_ISSUE_TEXT","note":null},{"issue_id":"PU_003","pdf_pages":[45],"layer":"ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE","knowledge_id":"PU_003_KNOW_025","source_file":"PU3/PU_003_COMPLETE_INGEST/PU_003_ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE.jsonl","source_authority":"DIRECT_ISSUE_TEXT","note":null},{"issue_id":"PU_005","pdf_pages":[13],"layer":"ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE","knowledge_id":"PU_005_KNOW_009","source_file":"PU5/PU_005_COMPLETE_INGEST/PU_005_ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE.jsonl","source_authority":"DIRECT_ISSUE_TEXT","note":null},{"issue_id":"PU_005","pdf_pages":[13],"layer":"ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE","knowledge_id":"PU_005_KNOW_010","source_file":"PU5/PU_005_COMPLETE_INGEST/PU_005_ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE.jsonl","source_authority":"DIRECT_ISSUE_TEXT","note":null}],"retrieval_policy":"Use as query router/summary; resolve important claims against evidence source layers."}
{"chunk_id":"RAG_PU_1993_HW_JAGUAR","publication_year":1993,"chunk_type":"HARDWARE_ARC","title":"Atari Jaguar","text":"Jaguar begins as a 64-bit rumor/report, is described in issue 2 with an onboard double-speed compact disc, is challenged by a reader in issue 3 and reframed as cartridge hardware with optional CD expansion, then becomes a confirmed hands-on machine in issue 5.","authority":"DERIVED_YEAR_SYNTHESIS","epistemic_status":"MIXED_DIRECT_FACT_AND_CROSS_ISSUE_SYNTHESIS","evidence":[{"issue_id":"PU_001","pdf_page":11,"layer":"BEST_MACHINE_TRANSCRIPT_BY_PAGE","source_file":"auth/PU1/BLACKPAPER_PU_001_COMPLETE_ARCHIVE_v2/raw_text/PU_001_BEST_MACHINE_TRANSCRIPT_BY_PAGE.jsonl","note":null},{"issue_id":"PU_002","pdf_pages":[16],"layer":"ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE","knowledge_id":"PU_002_KNOW_009","source_file":"auth/PU2/PU_002_COMPLETE_INGEST/PU_002_ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE.jsonl","source_authority":"DIRECT_ISSUE_TEXT","note":null},{"issue_id":"PU_003","pdf_page":8,"layer":"PAGE_TRANSCRIPTS","source_file":"PU3/PU_003_COMPLETE_INGEST/PU_003_PAGE_TRANSCRIPTS.jsonl","note":"reader correction/challenge"},{"issue_id":"PU_003","pdf_pages":[14],"layer":"ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE","knowledge_id":"PU_003_KNOW_010","source_file":"PU3/PU_003_COMPLETE_INGEST/PU_003_ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE.jsonl","source_authority":"DIRECT_ISSUE_TEXT","note":null},{"issue_id":"PU_005","pdf_pages":[15],"layer":"ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE","knowledge_id":"PU_005_KNOW_017","source_file":"PU5/PU_005_COMPLETE_INGEST/PU_005_ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE.jsonl","source_authority":"DIRECT_ISSUE_TEXT","note":null},{"issue_id":"PU_005","pdf_pages":[15],"layer":"ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE","knowledge_id":"PU_005_KNOW_018","source_file":"PU5/PU_005_COMPLETE_INGEST/PU_005_ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE.jsonl","source_authority":"DIRECT_ISSUE_TEXT","note":null}],"retrieval_policy":"Use as query router/summary; resolve important claims against evidence source layers."}
{"chunk_id":"RAG_PU_1993_HW_VR","publication_year":1993,"chunk_type":"HARDWARE_ARC","title":"Virtual Reality","text":"The corpus does not contain one unified PU position on VR. Issue 2 contains both near-term Sega VR expectation and a positive long-term prediction after a primitive demo; issue 3 prints Laurens Stolker rejecting VR; issue 4 prints Edward Laauwen predicting VR games as the future. These voices must remain distinct.","authority":"DERIVED_YEAR_SYNTHESIS","epistemic_status":"DIRECTLY_OBSERVED_CONTRADICTION_OF_VOICES","evidence":[{"issue_id":"PU_002","pdf_pages":[17],"layer":"ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE","knowledge_id":"PU_002_KNOW_010","source_file":"auth/PU2/PU_002_COMPLETE_INGEST/PU_002_ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE.jsonl","source_authority":"DIRECT_ISSUE_TEXT","note":null},{"issue_id":"PU_002","pdf_pages":[23],"layer":"ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE","knowledge_id":"PU_002_KNOW_023","source_file":"auth/PU2/PU_002_COMPLETE_INGEST/PU_002_ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE.jsonl","source_authority":"DIRECT_ISSUE_TEXT","note":null},{"issue_id":"PU_003","pdf_pages":[45],"layer":"ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE","knowledge_id":"PU_003_KNOW_025","source_file":"PU3/PU_003_COMPLETE_INGEST/PU_003_ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE.jsonl","source_authority":"DIRECT_ISSUE_TEXT","note":null},{"issue_id":"PU_004","pdf_pages":[65],"layer":"ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE","knowledge_id":"PU_004_KNOW_037","source_file":"PU4/PU_004_COMPLETE_INGEST/PU_004_ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE.jsonl","source_authority":"DIRECT_ISSUE_TEXT","note":null}],"retrieval_policy":"Use as query router/summary; resolve important claims against evidence source layers."}
{"chunk_id":"RAG_PU_1993_HW_CD32","publication_year":1993,"chunk_type":"HARDWARE_ARC","title":"Amiga CD32","text":"CD32 becomes visible partly through reader pressure: an Amiga reader criticizes PU for overlooking the platform, PU says it will wait and speak to Commodore, and the same issue contains substantive CD32 coverage describing it as a 32-bit CD console already in shops.","authority":"DERIVED_YEAR_SYNTHESIS","epistemic_status":"DIRECT_SEQUENCE_WITH_SYNTHESIS","evidence":[{"issue_id":"PU_003","pdf_pages":[8,9],"layer":"ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE","knowledge_id":"PU_003_KNOW_003","source_file":"PU3/PU_003_COMPLETE_INGEST/PU_003_ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE.jsonl","source_authority":"DIRECT_ISSUE_TEXT","note":null},{"issue_id":"PU_003","pdf_pages":[9],"layer":"ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE","knowledge_id":"PU_003_KNOW_004","source_file":"PU3/PU_003_COMPLETE_INGEST/PU_003_ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE.jsonl","source_authority":"DIRECT_ISSUE_TEXT","note":null},{"issue_id":"PU_003","pdf_pages":[15],"layer":"ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE","knowledge_id":"PU_003_KNOW_014","source_file":"PU3/PU_003_COMPLETE_INGEST/PU_003_ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE.jsonl","source_authority":"DIRECT_ISSUE_TEXT","note":null}],"retrieval_policy":"Use as query router/summary; resolve important claims against evidence source layers."}
{"chunk_id":"RAG_PU_1993_FEEDBACK_PREVIEW_TERM","publication_year":1993,"chunk_type":"READER_FEEDBACK_LOOP","title":"PREVIEW terminology","text":"A reader in issue 2 challenges the use of PREVIEW for import games. PU then repeatedly publishes a house definition in which REVIEW/BESPREKING tracks broad Dutch availability and PREVIEW/VOORBESPREKING tracks specialist/import/rental availability.","authority":"DERIVED_YEAR_SYNTHESIS","epistemic_status":"DIRECT_EDITORIAL_POLICY_CONTINUITY","evidence":[{"issue_id":"PU_002","pdf_pages":[8],"layer":"ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE","knowledge_id":"PU_002_KNOW_002","source_file":"auth/PU2/PU_002_COMPLETE_INGEST/PU_002_ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE.jsonl","source_authority":"DIRECT_ISSUE_TEXT","note":null},{"issue_id":"PU_002","pdf_pages":[19],"layer":"ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE","knowledge_id":"PU_002_KNOW_015","source_file":"auth/PU2/PU_002_COMPLETE_INGEST/PU_002_ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE.jsonl","source_authority":"DIRECT_ISSUE_TEXT","note":null},{"issue_id":"PU_003","pdf_pages":[19],"layer":"ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE","knowledge_id":"PU_003_KNOW_018","source_file":"PU3/PU_003_COMPLETE_INGEST/PU_003_ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE.jsonl","source_authority":"DIRECT_ISSUE_TEXT","note":null},{"issue_id":"PU_003","pdf_pages":[19],"layer":"ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE","knowledge_id":"PU_003_KNOW_019","source_file":"PU3/PU_003_COMPLETE_INGEST/PU_003_ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE.jsonl","source_authority":"DIRECT_ISSUE_TEXT","note":null},{"issue_id":"PU_004","pdf_pages":[19],"layer":"ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE","knowledge_id":"PU_004_KNOW_016","source_file":"PU4/PU_004_COMPLETE_INGEST/PU_004_ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE.jsonl","source_authority":"DIRECT_ISSUE_TEXT","note":null},{"issue_id":"PU_004","pdf_pages":[19],"layer":"ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE","knowledge_id":"PU_004_KNOW_017","source_file":"PU4/PU_004_COMPLETE_INGEST/PU_004_ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE.jsonl","source_authority":"DIRECT_ISSUE_TEXT","note":null},{"issue_id":"PU_005","pdf_page":19,"layer":"PAGE_TRANSCRIPTS","source_file":"PU5/PU_005_COMPLETE_INGEST/PU_005_PAGE_TRANSCRIPTS.jsonl","note":null}],"retrieval_policy":"Use as query router/summary; resolve important claims against evidence source layers."}
{"chunk_id":"RAG_PU_1993_FEEDBACK_MARIO_KART","publication_year":1993,"chunk_type":"READER_FEEDBACK_LOOP","title":"Super Mario Kart","text":"Bjorn scores Super Mario Kart 6.5 in issue 1. Issue 2 publishes reader disagreement. Issue 4 explicitly says the earlier judgement produced many angry reactions and revisits the game in Eeuwig Leven. No replacement score is printed, so this is a re-evaluation framing rather than a score correction.","authority":"DERIVED_YEAR_SYNTHESIS","epistemic_status":"DIRECT_SEQUENCE_WITH_CAUSAL_LANGUAGE_IN_SOURCE","evidence":[{"issue_id":"PU_001","pdf_pages":[55,55],"layer":"PU_001_CONSOLIDATED_REVIEW_CANON_v1.1","year_review_id":"PU_1993_REVIEW_028","source_record_id":"PU_001_CONSOLIDATED_028","note":null},{"issue_id":"PU_002","pdf_page":11,"layer":"PAGE_TRANSCRIPTS","source_file":"auth/PU2/PU_002_COMPLETE_INGEST/PU_002_PAGE_TRANSCRIPTS.jsonl","note":null},{"issue_id":"PU_004","pdf_pages":[67],"layer":"ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE","knowledge_id":"PU_004_KNOW_032","source_file":"PU4/PU_004_COMPLETE_INGEST/PU_004_ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE.jsonl","source_authority":"DIRECT_ISSUE_TEXT","note":null}],"retrieval_policy":"Use as query router/summary; resolve important claims against evidence source layers."}
{"chunk_id":"RAG_PU_1993_FEEDBACK_LOST_VIKINGS","publication_year":1993,"chunk_type":"READER_FEEDBACK_LOOP","title":"The Lost Vikings","text":"The Lost Vikings becomes a months-long reader/editor knowledge loop: the issue 2 review is followed by issue 3 reader-supplied endgame codes after Bjorn became stuck, issue 4 reader complaints about promised codes, and issue 5 another reader solution for level 38.","authority":"DERIVED_YEAR_SYNTHESIS","epistemic_status":"DIRECT_CROSS_ISSUE_CONTINUITY","evidence":[{"issue_id":"PU_002","pdf_page":24,"layer":"PAGE_TRANSCRIPTS","source_file":"auth/PU2/PU_002_COMPLETE_INGEST/PU_002_PAGE_TRANSCRIPTS.jsonl","note":null},{"issue_id":"PU_003","pdf_page":66,"layer":"PAGE_TRANSCRIPTS","source_file":"PU3/PU_003_COMPLETE_INGEST/PU_003_PAGE_TRANSCRIPTS.jsonl","note":null},{"issue_id":"PU_004","pdf_pages":[9],"layer":"ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE","knowledge_id":"PU_004_KNOW_004","source_file":"PU4/PU_004_COMPLETE_INGEST/PU_004_ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE.jsonl","source_authority":"DIRECT_ISSUE_TEXT","note":null},{"issue_id":"PU_005","pdf_page":69,"layer":"PAGE_TRANSCRIPTS","source_file":"PU5/PU_005_COMPLETE_INGEST/PU_005_PAGE_TRANSCRIPTS.jsonl","note":null}],"retrieval_policy":"Use as query router/summary; resolve important claims against evidence source layers."}
{"chunk_id":"RAG_PU_1993_FEEDBACK_ASTERIX_REQUEST","publication_year":1993,"chunk_type":"READER_FEEDBACK_LOOP","title":"Asterix","text":"Issue 3 records a reader request asking PU to put Asterix on Super NES in that very issue; the issue contains scored Asterix evaluations. This shows the letters layer and review layer intersecting, although timing does not prove the letter caused the review.","authority":"DERIVED_YEAR_SYNTHESIS","epistemic_status":"COINCIDENCE_OR_POSSIBLE_EDITORIAL_RESPONSE_NOT_PROVEN","evidence":[{"issue_id":"PU_003","pdf_pages":[9],"layer":"ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE","knowledge_id":"PU_003_KNOW_005","source_file":"PU3/PU_003_COMPLETE_INGEST/PU_003_ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE.jsonl","source_authority":"DIRECT_ISSUE_TEXT","note":null},{"issue_id":"PU_003","pdf_pages":[24,25],"layer":"HUMAN_CANON_REVIEWS","year_review_id":"PU_1993_REVIEW_087","source_record_id":"PU_003_REVIEW_003","note":null}],"retrieval_policy":"Use as query router/summary; resolve important claims against evidence source layers."}
{"chunk_id":"RAG_PU_1993_PRC_001","publication_year":1993,"chunk_type":"PREDICTION_REVISION_CONTRADICTION","title":"3DO","text":"Issue 5 explicitly recalls earlier caution about 3DO and then reports a working machine with software, making this an internally documented revision of confidence.","authority":"DERIVED_YEAR_SYNTHESIS","epistemic_status":"DERIVED_SYNTHESIS","evidence":[{"issue_id":"PU_005","pdf_pages":[13],"layer":"ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE","knowledge_id":"PU_005_KNOW_010","source_file":"PU5/PU_005_COMPLETE_INGEST/PU_005_ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE.jsonl","source_authority":"DIRECT_ISSUE_TEXT","note":null},{"issue_id":"PU_005","pdf_pages":[13],"layer":"ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE","knowledge_id":"PU_005_KNOW_009","source_file":"PU5/PU_005_COMPLETE_INGEST/PU_005_ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE.jsonl","source_authority":"DIRECT_ISSUE_TEXT","note":null}],"retrieval_policy":"Use as query router/summary; resolve important claims against evidence source layers."}
{"chunk_id":"RAG_PU_1993_PRC_002","publication_year":1993,"chunk_type":"PREDICTION_REVISION_CONTRADICTION","title":"Atari Jaguar CD configuration","text":"Issue 2 says Jaguar contains a double-speed compact disc; issue 3 reader feedback disputes this, and later coverage treats CD as an expansion/add-on rather than the core cartridge medium.","authority":"DERIVED_YEAR_SYNTHESIS","epistemic_status":"DERIVED_SYNTHESIS","evidence":[{"issue_id":"PU_002","pdf_pages":[16],"layer":"ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE","knowledge_id":"PU_002_KNOW_009","source_file":"auth/PU2/PU_002_COMPLETE_INGEST/PU_002_ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE.jsonl","source_authority":"DIRECT_ISSUE_TEXT","note":null},{"issue_id":"PU_003","pdf_page":8,"layer":"PAGE_TRANSCRIPTS","source_file":"PU3/PU_003_COMPLETE_INGEST/PU_003_PAGE_TRANSCRIPTS.jsonl","note":null},{"issue_id":"PU_003","pdf_page":14,"layer":"PAGE_TRANSCRIPTS","source_file":"PU3/PU_003_COMPLETE_INGEST/PU_003_PAGE_TRANSCRIPTS.jsonl","note":null},{"issue_id":"PU_005","pdf_pages":[15],"layer":"ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE","knowledge_id":"PU_005_KNOW_017","source_file":"PU5/PU_005_COMPLETE_INGEST/PU_005_ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE.jsonl","source_authority":"DIRECT_ISSUE_TEXT","note":null}],"retrieval_policy":"Use as query router/summary; resolve important claims against evidence source layers."}
{"chunk_id":"RAG_PU_1993_PRC_003","publication_year":1993,"chunk_type":"PREDICTION_REVISION_CONTRADICTION","title":"Virtual Reality future","text":"Positive and negative future claims coexist across different speakers and articles. YEAR_SYNTHESIS must not collapse them into a single PU prediction.","authority":"DERIVED_YEAR_SYNTHESIS","epistemic_status":"DERIVED_SYNTHESIS","evidence":[{"issue_id":"PU_002","pdf_pages":[23],"layer":"ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE","knowledge_id":"PU_002_KNOW_023","source_file":"auth/PU2/PU_002_COMPLETE_INGEST/PU_002_ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE.jsonl","source_authority":"DIRECT_ISSUE_TEXT","note":null},{"issue_id":"PU_003","pdf_pages":[45],"layer":"ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE","knowledge_id":"PU_003_KNOW_025","source_file":"PU3/PU_003_COMPLETE_INGEST/PU_003_ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE.jsonl","source_authority":"DIRECT_ISSUE_TEXT","note":null},{"issue_id":"PU_004","pdf_pages":[65],"layer":"ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE","knowledge_id":"PU_004_KNOW_037","source_file":"PU4/PU_004_COMPLETE_INGEST/PU_004_ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE.jsonl","source_authority":"DIRECT_ISSUE_TEXT","note":null}],"retrieval_policy":"Use as query router/summary; resolve important claims against evidence source layers."}
{"chunk_id":"RAG_PU_1993_PRC_004","publication_year":1993,"chunk_type":"PREDICTION_REVISION_CONTRADICTION","title":"Project Reality","text":"Issue 5 carries a prediction that Project Reality would bring Jurassic Park-like technology into the home within about two years. This package records the prediction only and does not test it against external reality.","authority":"DERIVED_YEAR_SYNTHESIS","epistemic_status":"DERIVED_SYNTHESIS","evidence":[{"issue_id":"PU_005","pdf_pages":[65],"layer":"ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE","knowledge_id":"PU_005_KNOW_030","source_file":"PU5/PU_005_COMPLETE_INGEST/PU_005_ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE.jsonl","source_authority":"DIRECT_ISSUE_TEXT","note":null}],"retrieval_policy":"Use as query router/summary; resolve important claims against evidence source layers."}
{"chunk_id":"RAG_PU_1993_PRC_005","publication_year":1993,"chunk_type":"PREDICTION_REVISION_CONTRADICTION","title":"Mortal Kombat / Ermac","text":"Issue 5 reports Ermac as a mysterious player anecdote and explicitly asks readers to help investigate. The synthesis preserves it as a contemporary mystery report, not established game fact.","authority":"DERIVED_YEAR_SYNTHESIS","epistemic_status":"DERIVED_SYNTHESIS","evidence":[{"issue_id":"PU_005","pdf_pages":[16],"layer":"ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE","knowledge_id":"PU_005_KNOW_019","source_file":"PU5/PU_005_COMPLETE_INGEST/PU_005_ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE.jsonl","source_authority":"DIRECT_ISSUE_TEXT","note":null},{"issue_id":"PU_005","pdf_pages":[16],"layer":"ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE","knowledge_id":"PU_005_KNOW_020","source_file":"PU5/PU_005_COMPLETE_INGEST/PU_005_ISSUE_KNOWLEDGE.jsonl","source_authority":"DIRECT_ISSUE_TEXT","note":null}],"retrieval_policy":"Use as query router/summary; resolve important claims against evidence source layers."}
{"chunk_id":"RAG_PU_1993_EDITOR_001","publication_year":1993,"chunk_type":"EDITOR_CONTINUITY","title":"Core redaction expansion","text":"Issue 1 masthead lists Bjorn Bruinsma, Ben de Dood, Adam Eeuwens, Kees de Koning and David Lemereis under Redaktie, while Michael Schaeffer is a contributor. Issue 2 adds Michael to Redaktie, and issues 3-5 keep a six-person core.","authority":"DERIVED_YEAR_SYNTHESIS","epistemic_status":"DIRECT_MASTHEAD_CONTINUITY","evidence":[{"issue_id":"PU_001","pdf_page":5,"layer":"PU_001_MASTHEAD","source_file":"auth/PU1/BLACKPAPER_PU_001_COMPLETE_ARCHIVE_v2/canon/PU_001_MASTHEAD.json"},{"issue_id":"PU_002","pdf_page":5,"layer":"PAGE_TRANSCRIPTS","source_file":"auth/PU2/PU_002_COMPLETE_INGEST/PU_002_PAGE_TRANSCRIPTS.jsonl","note":null},{"issue_id":"PU_003","pdf_page":5,"layer":"PAGE_TRANSCRIPTS","source_file":"PU3/PU_003_COMPLETE_INGEST/PU_003_PAGE_TRANSCRIPTS.jsonl","note":null},{"issue_id":"PU_004","pdf_page":5,"layer":"PAGE_TRANSCRIPTS","source_file":"PU4/PU_004_COMPLETE_INGEST/PU_004_PAGE_TRANSCRIPTS.jsonl","note":null},{"issue_id":"PU_005","pdf_page":5,"layer":"PAGE_TRANSCRIPTS","source_file":"PU5/PU_005_COMPLETE_INGEST/PU_005_PAGE_TRANSCRIPTS.jsonl","note":null}],"retrieval_policy":"Use as query router/summary; resolve important claims against evidence source layers."}
{"chunk_id":"RAG_PU_1993_EDITOR_002","publication_year":1993,"chunk_type":"EDITOR_CONTINUITY","title":"Michael surname spelling","text":"The corpus spells the editor/contributor surname Schaeffer in issue 1 and issues 3-5, but Schaefer in issue 2. YEAR_SYNTHESIS groups these only for inferred year-level statistics and preserves every source spelling.","authority":"DERIVED_YEAR_SYNTHESIS","epistemic_status":"DIRECT_SPELLING_VARIATION_PLUS_IDENTITY_INFERENCE","evidence":[{"issue_id":"PU_001","pdf_page":5,"layer":"PU_001_MASTHEAD","source_file":"auth/PU1/BLACKPAPER_PU_001_COMPLETE_ARCHIVE_v2/canon/PU_001_MASTHEAD.json"},{"issue_id":"PU_002","pdf_page":5,"layer":"PAGE_TRANSCRIPTS","source_file":"auth/PU2/PU_002_COMPLETE_INGEST/PU_002_PAGE_TRANSCRIPTS.jsonl","note":null},{"issue_id":"PU_003","pdf_page":5,"layer":"PAGE_TRANSCRIPTS","source_file":"PU3/PU_003_COMPLETE_INGEST/PU_003_PAGE_TRANSCRIPTS.jsonl","note":null},{"issue_id":"PU_004","pdf_page":5,"layer":"PAGE_TRANSCRIPTS","source_file":"PU4/PU_004_COMPLETE_INGEST/PU_004_PAGE_TRANSCRIPTS.jsonl","note":null},{"issue_id":"PU_005","pdf_page":5,"layer":"PAGE_TRANSCRIPTS","source_file":"PU5/PU_005_COMPLETE_INGEST/PU_005_PAGE_TRANSCRIPTS.jsonl","note":null}],"retrieval_policy":"Use as query router/summary; resolve important claims against evidence source layers."}
{"chunk_id":"RAG_PU_1993_REVIEWER_RANGE","publication_year":1993,"chunk_type":"REVIEWER_PROFILE","title":"Reviewer scoring profiles","text":"Among inferred single-reviewer identity groups with at least five scored evaluations, Michael Schaeffer has the lowest mean (7.388/10, n=25) and David Lemereis the highest (8.400/10, n=21). Joint bylines are excluded and Michael Schaefer/Schaeffer is an explicit year-level identity inference.","authority":"DERIVED_YEAR_SYNTHESIS","epistemic_status":"DERIVED_STATISTIC","evidence":[],"retrieval_policy":"Use as query router/summary; resolve important claims against evidence source layers."}
{"chunk_id":"RAG_PU_1993_LARGEST_PLATFORM_SPREAD","publication_year":1993,"chunk_type":"PLATFORM_COMPARISON","title":"Largest within-issue platform score spread","text":"The largest exact-title within-issue platform spread in the year review canon is Spider-Man in PU_004: 2.5 points on the 10-point scale.","authority":"DERIVED_YEAR_SYNTHESIS","epistemic_status":"DERIVED_STATISTIC","evidence":[{"year_review_id":"PU_1993_REVIEW_128"},{"year_review_id":"PU_1993_REVIEW_129"},{"year_review_id":"PU_1993_REVIEW_130"},{"year_review_id":"PU_1993_REVIEW_131"}],"retrieval_policy":"Use as query router/summary; resolve important claims against evidence source layers."}
